WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.11 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Reporting and communicating evidence

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Each audience needs its own report, honest from the very first one.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.170
Reporting shares your evidence with the people who need it, in a form each can use. Different audiences need different reports, but every one of them needs honesty.

4
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.170
Different audiences, different reports

5
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:34.537
Co-founders and advisers: A short dashboard and the main risks. For example: One page each quarter: five indicators, traffic lights and two risks.

6
00:00:34.537 --> 00:00:42.533
Funders: Agreed formats and deadlines. For example: The six-month report the local youth fund asked for, in its own template.

7
00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:51.641
Customers and members: What their support or purchases achieved. For example: A yearly note to our café and canteen buyers: what their orders made possible.

8
00:00:51.641 --> 00:01:03.430
Participants and public: Accessible feedback and honest, simple stories backed by evidence. For example: A poster at the stall: what we learned from the pilot and what we changed.

9
00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.430
Why it matters

10
00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:10.104
1. A new initiative builds credibility when its claims match its data.

11
00:01:10.104 --> 00:01:15.037
2. Reporting what did not work shows that you learn.

12
00:01:15.037 --> 00:01:21.341
3. Reusing one set of data saves time for every audience.

13
00:01:21.741 --> 00:01:22.341
Where it goes next

14
00:01:22.341 --> 00:01:28.015
1. Your MEAL calendar: each report has a date and an owner.

15
00:01:28.015 --> 00:01:32.207
2. Your communications: evidence becomes messages and stories.

16
00:01:32.207 --> 00:01:38.881
3. The fuller reports funders, members or customers will ask for later.

17
00:01:39.281 --> 00:01:39.881
What to avoid

18
00:01:39.881 --> 00:01:44.074
Presenting outputs as if they were outcomes.

19
00:01:44.074 --> 00:01:49.007
Claiming you caused a change you only contributed to.

20
00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:54.570
Recreating the data from scratch for every report.

21
00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.970
You build your reporting plan by audience.

22
00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.970
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.570
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
